In Finland, inflation was 0.2 per cent minus-marking according to the EU's harmonised price index.
Inflation in the euro area remains persistently far from the European Central Bank (ECB) target of 2% higher prices over the medium term.
The ECB predicts an average inflation of 0.1 per cent for the eurozone this year.
As of next year, the surge will budge to 1.1 per cent, the central bank anticipates in its new inflation projections released in early September.
