The grocery stall within the store (good, cheap) is close to coffers, with a number of take-out options.
What's in the warehouse: Do you need something - anything - Thai?
LAX-C will probably sell it.
The products are reasonably priced, and a large proportion of products are sold in wholesale packaging.
The fresh products include Asian specialties and regional Thai herbs, fruit and other products.
Meat distension is a large fish distension. The staff behind the counter clean and fillet the fish and, if necessary, fry it for you.
A big chunk of the store is earmarked for a huge frozen truncated curry leaf, bitter cucumber and galangalia, complete ducks, fish, beef meat and bile, pork leather, fishball, local sausculptors, foods and more.
Who goes to the store: Restaurant owners and chefs, but also individual families and individuals.
For wide corridors, shopping trolleys as well as trunks are suitable.
Finding: A recent monthong duriot next to the checkout.
Where it's located: The store is in a Los Angeles factory area near Chinatown and downtown stair stations - a few blocks from Philippe The Original.
Parking: LAX-C has its own parking area, which it distributes with other shops and restaurants.
Even though it can be a busy shop, it's usually easy to find a parking spot.
